Keys for German:

  <ss> and <SS> and <ae oe ue> and <Ae Oe Ue> and <AE OE UE>

HTML entities work as keys as well:

  <szlig> and <7838> and <auml ouml uuml> and <Auml Ouml Uuml>

The Unicode codepoints for the German Eszett (sharp s) are U+00DF for
the lowercase letter and U+1E9E for the capital letter.

A classic German tongue-twister (Zungenbrecher) packed with ä, ö, ü,
and ß:

    „Hinter Herrenhäusern kreisen krächzende Krähen, 
    während süße, 
    mürbe Gänslein große Ölfässer umstoßen.“

    <bdquo>Hinter Herrenh<ae>usern kreisen kr<ae>chzende Kr<ae>hen,
    w<ae>hrend s<ue><ss>e,
    m<ue>rbe G<ae>nslein gro<ss>e <Oe>lf<ae>sser umsto<ss>en.<ldquo>

📝 English Translation

   "Behind mansions circle croaking crows, while sweet, tender little
   geese knock over large oil barrels."
